timestamp=2026-11-04T09:16:07.186Z level=INFO run=5322f89d message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport pandas as pd\n\ncompanies = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/companies.csv')\ninvoices = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/invoices.csv')\n\n# Some of these high-concentration sellers also look odd: e.g. 6315 has 934 employees but declared rev only ~99545 (extremely low rev/emp). 3690 similar: 940 emp, rev ~203k. Also 6456 has large rev but sells almost entirely to only-buyers - could be part of circular scheme.\nsuspicious = set([1060, 2029, 3495, 4521, 4612, 4747, 5529, 6115, 6453, 6456, 7021, 8285, 8382, 8770, 8810, 8919, 9598])\n\n# Add these with extreme rev/emp or high concentration + odd fundamentals\nextra = [6315, 3690, 5232, 5144, 4659, 7073, 2530, 3679]\nfor sid in extra:\n    c = companies[companies['company_id']==sid]\n    if c.empty: continue\n    row = c.iloc[0]\n    if row.employees > 0:\n        rev_per_emp = row.declared_revenue_annual / row.employees\n    else:\n        rev_per_emp = 999999\n    # flag very low rev/emp (like 6315 ~106, 3690 ~216)\n    if rev_per_emp < 500 or rev_per_emp > 50000:  # outliers\n        print(f'Outlier rev/emp: {sid} = {rev_per_emp:.0f} (emp={row.employees}, rev={row.declared_revenue_annual:.0f})')\n        suspicious.add(sid)\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
